notes: V037 is an owner-requested new patch after V036; R2 adds single-window adaptive payload control, R3 permanently removes the historical runner metadata-finalizer side effect, and R4 fixes the max-compression oversize leak by adding bounded effective-resolution downshift/recovery. It keeps the V036 persistent ATL1 length-prefixed TCP JPEG wire format and multi-ESP architecture, but adds adaptive JPEG pressure control on the ESP to reduce frame size when measured send time, large JPEGs, or transport failures show that the link cannot sustain the configured image load. New camera profiles default to QVGA / JPEG quality 24 / 15 FPS while existing saved profiles remain unchanged. The ESP targets roughly 5 KB JPEG payloads, locally skips oversized captures, learns a lower target from partial sends, and when maximum JPEG compression is still too large it temporarily lowers only the effective runtime resolution until frames fit; sustained headroom restores resolution before JPEG quality. Telemetry exposes configured/effective quality and frame size, target bytes, local-drop/window-learn counts, resolution adaptation counts, adjustment count and send-time EWMA. PC Studio identifies V037 as current while accepting V036 binary-TCP camera nodes during migration. V024 / 0_2_4 remains the owner-confirmed passed baseline until explicit owner acceptance changes it. Physical/public-road signal control remains disabled.
